<title>INDIA: India's Grasim raises $18 mln loan.</title>
<headline>India's Grasim raises $18 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Grasim Industries Ltd has raised a four-year $18 million syndicated term facility arranged by ANZ Investment Bank and Standard Chartered Bank, one of the arrangers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>ANZ said in a statement that the loan was Grasim's first Euro currency borrowing and would be used to finance the modernisation and towards the normal capital expenditure relating to the company's rayon plant at Mavoor in Kerala Harihar in Karnataka.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
